 # Changelog
 
+## 0.4.5 (unreleased)
+
+Not compiled or run when written (edit-only pass); CI is the compiler. Additive only: no existing public item changes, so dependents (rightkit-browser, rightkit-onnx) need no republish.
+
+- **`GpuDetail`: raw VRAM in MiB and the reporting probe (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#709, for CodeRight).** `Gpu` is unchanged. New `GpuDetail { gpu, vram_mib: Option<u64>, source: Option<String> }` (`vram_mib` is the unrounded probe value, so 16376 MiB stays 16376 where `vram_gb` rounds to 0.1 GB; `source` is one of `GpuDetail::SOURCE_NVIDIA_SMI`, `SOURCE_WMIC`, `SOURCE_SYSTEM_PROFILER`, `SOURCE_REGISTRY`, `None` for a synthesized Apple Silicon entry). Returned by `Hardware::detect_detailed()` and `Hardware::probe_with_runner_detailed(runner)` as `(Hardware, Vec<GpuDetail>)`, where `details[i]` describes `hw.gpus[i]`, and by the pure parsers `parse_nvidia_smi_csv_detailed`, `parse_wmic_video_detailed` and `parse_system_profiler_displays_detailed`. `detect`, `probe_with_runner` and the existing parsers behave as before (they are the detailed versions without the extras). A duplicate-name merge fills `vram_mib` and `source` together with the VRAM. Tests: `probe.rs` (`detailed_parsers_keep_raw_mib_and_the_reporting_probe`, the merge test).
+- **`DownloadSource` and `ensure_ready_from_source` (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#727, for MailRight).** A caller-chosen route for a pinned model: a base URL for `SpecSource::Files` models (`<base>/<path>`, also for files whose catalog `url` is `None`, such as the EmbeddingGemma 2 Q4 bundle) or the archive URL for `SpecSource::Archive`. Digest and size pins are unchanged and still enforced, so a mirror can only supply the right bytes. The app bearer and worker grants are never sent to the source; a catalog `requires_auth` model downloads from it without one. `DownloadSource::new` accepts `http(s)://host/...` only, refuses user information, query, fragment and whitespace. `ModelStore::with_download_source` / `download_source`; `ModelStore::ensure` uses it and then skips grants (`ensure_entitled` is unaffected). `suite::ensure_ready_from_source` is the free-function form. `FileSpec::mirrors` for the manifest `Store` already existed (0.4.3 content). No environment variable is read here. Tests: `tests/download_source_status.rs`.
+- **Serializable `ModelStatus` and `effective_dir_at` (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#741 item 1, for ScrapeRight).** `ModelStatus`, `SetStatus`, `EntryState` and `ModelTier` derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize` (`state` and `tier` snake_case). New `suite::effective_dir_at(models_root, spec, siblings, seed_entry_dir) -> Option<EffectiveModelDir { dir, source }>` and `ModelStore::effective_dir`: shared entry, then sibling entries (machine-wide root only), then the seed entry directory; each must be `Ready` at `VerifyMode::Size` against the trusted manifest. Read-only. Tests: `tests/download_source_status.rs`.
+- **Not done here.** #741 item 2 (case-insensitive `find_processes`) is `rightkit-child-process`, not this crate. #542 (LLMLingua spec) needs a hosted route and pinned digests that do not exist (see the report).
+
 ## 0.4.4 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **New: `suite::archive::install_tar_gz_expecting(archive, dest_root, expected_wrapper, installed_name)`** (Orthic-Labs/rightkit#455). Same atomic install as `install_tar_gz`, but the archive's single top-level directory must be named exactly `expected_wrapper`; another name or a second top-level entry is refused before installation, leaving the previous install untouched and no staging directory behind. `install_tar_gz` is unchanged and shares the implementation. Additive; version not bumped here. Tests: `tests/install_tar_gz_expecting.rs`. Not compiled when written.
