 - **Licence.** To be confirmed. The existing specs in this catalog carry no licence field, and
   none was sourced for this bundle.
 
+## Download source, serializable status and effective directory (0.4.5)
+
+- `DownloadSource::new(url)` names where to fetch a pinned model from instead of its catalog URL (a mirror), or when the catalog has none (the EmbeddingGemma 2 Q4 bundle). For a per-file model the value is a base URL (`<base>/<file path>`); for an archive model it is the archive URL. The pins stay: every file must match its SHA-256 and size, so a source can only supply the right bytes. The app's bearer and any worker grant are never sent to it. Use `ModelStore::with_download_source(source)` (then `ensure` downloads from it) or `suite::ensure_ready_from_source`. The crate reads no environment variable: the app reads its own setting and passes the value.
+- `ModelStatus`, `SetStatus`, `EntryState` and `ModelTier` implement `Serialize`/`Deserialize` (`state` and `tier` are snake_case strings), so no mirror DTO is needed.
+- `suite::effective_dir_at(models_root, spec, siblings, seed_entry_dir)` / `ModelStore::effective_dir` return the directory a model loads from now and whether it is the `shared`, a `sibling` or the `seed` copy (`EffectiveModelDir`). Read-only: no ref is registered (that stays with `ModelStore::resolve`).
+- `Hardware::detect_detailed()` / `Hardware::probe_with_runner_detailed(runner)` also return `Vec<GpuDetail>` (`gpu`, raw `vram_mib`, `source` naming the probe: `GpuDetail::SOURCE_NVIDIA_SMI`, `SOURCE_WMIC`, `SOURCE_SYSTEM_PROFILER`, `SOURCE_REGISTRY`), parallel to `Hardware::gpus`. `Gpu` itself is unchanged.
+
 ## EmbeddingGemma 2 E43 archive (route defined, pins required)
 
 E43 (int8 token table, batched ingest graphs; read by `rightkit-embed` 0.6.0) ships as one worker-served `.tar.gz` at `EMBEDDINGGEMMA2_E43_DML_URL`, verified against a whole-archive SHA-256 and size before extraction. The real digest and the per-file pins are not recorded in this repository, so `EMBEDDINGGEMMA2_E43_DML_PINS` is `None` and `embedding_gemma2_e43_dml_spec()` returns `Err(MissingE43Pins)`: nothing downloads an unpinned archive. Once the owner of the built archive supplies the pins, record them in `EMBEDDINGGEMMA2_E43_DML_PINS` (or build the spec with `embedding_gemma2_e43_dml_spec_with(EmbeddingGemma2E43Pins { .. })`). See bogusyogi/rightkit#224.
